hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18644","Waki narrated to us, al-Masudi narrated to us from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah from Usamah ibn Sharik, he said: I came to the Prophet and his companions were as if birds were upon their heads."
"18645","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah from Usamah ibn Sharik, he said: I came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and his companions were with him as if birds were upon their heads; he said: So I greeted him and sat; he said: Then Bedouins came and asked him, and they said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we seek treatment, he said: Yes, seek treatment, for Allah has placed no disease except He placed for it a cure, other than one disease: old age; he said: And Usamah, when he grew old, would say: Do you see any cure for me now; he said: And they asked him about things: Is there sin upon us in such and such, he said: O servants of Allah, Allah has removed sin, except a man who takes the due of a Muslim man unjustly, that is sin and ruin; they said: What is the best thing given to people, O Messenger of Allah, he said: Good character."
"18646","Ibn Ziyad, meaning al-Muttalib ibn Ziyad, narrated to us, Ziyad ibn Ilaqah narrated to us from Usamah ibn Sharik that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Seek treatment, O servants of Allah, for Allah, Mighty and Majestic, sent down no disease except He sent down healing with it, except death and old age."
"18647","Musab ibn Sallam narrated to us, al-Ajlah narrated to us from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah from Usamah ibn Sharik, a man of his people, he said: A Bedouin came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, which people are best, he said: The best of them in character; then he said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we seek treatment, he said: Seek treatment, for Allah sent down no disease except He sent down healing for it; whoever knows it knows it, and whoever is ignorant of it is ignorant of it."
